    "review_findings": [
      "All 32 fixed-scope file hashes match the scope manifest exactly; frozen research trio, canonical config/draft, root receipts, nine formal files, shared map/indexes and three reverse weapon pages are stable.",
      "The three actual trait families each define I–IV toughness_fixed_percentage 0.045/0.05/0.055/0.06 with percentage-plus formatting; each wrapper directly clones the common close-kill recovery buff without a later override. The tier percentage replaces the 0.02 fallback.",
      "The Traditional Chinese RAW says melee kill while the implementation requires a ranged death or count_as_ranged_attack; formal reconstruction preserves the exact wording and the errata identifies the contradiction. English omits attack type and exact range, correctly marked as undocumented.",
      "Eligibility is source-item and held-slot gated, requires a death and a ranged attack, and uses an inclusive 12.5 m hit-position distance. Rippergun bayonet/push/melee actions are excluded; P3’s actual special is a toggle with no special-shell wiring; P4 special direct pellets remain ranged, while P4 Mk III follow-up interval damage is a buff attack without count_as_ranged_attack and does not qualify.",
      "Recovery uses the current effective maximum toughness times the tier fraction, caps at current missing toughness, ignores toughness replenish modifiers via ignore_stat_buffs, and remains subject to the three recovery-prevention keywords and alive/downed conditions. The 2 s ProcBuff active window is not a cooldown, regeneration period, or stacking recovery effect; a processed eligible kill recovers immediately, and switching/window expiry does not undo recovered toughness.",
      "The M=200 examples are arithmetically correct: III with 20 missing restores 11; IV with 5 missing calculates 12 but restores only 5. Map values, 3 variants/6 bindings, item restrictions, UI names, icon 059 attachment, and all reverse links agree with the formal pages and receipts."
    ],
